Changes to upstream files
-------------------------
The port modifies a small number of upstream C/C++ files. Every change is guarded by
#ifdef _WIN32 / __APPLE__, leaves Windows behaviour unchanged, and is listed with its reason in
Mac/docs/upstream-patches.md (exact diff: Mac/docs/upstream-patches.diff).

Bundled assets from the official 7-Zip release
----------------------------------------------
Taken unmodified from the official 7-Zip 26.03 Windows release (7z2603-x64.exe, verified by
SHA-256 in Mac/scripts/fetch-assets.sh), Copyright (C) Igor Pavlov and, for the translations, their
respective translators:

  - Mac/Resources/Help/        the help pages (HTML and CSS) unpacked from 7-zip.chm
  - Mac/Resources/Lang/        the 93 translation files (Lang/*.txt, Lang/en.ttt)
  - Mac/Resources/SFX/         the Windows self-extracting archive modules 7z.sfx and 7zCon.sfx,
                               with the release's License.txt and readme.txt

Icons
-----
The app icon, the document icons and the toolbar images are converted from the original 7-Zip
icon and bitmap files in the upstream source tree: CPP/7zip/Archive/Icons/*.ico and
CPP/7zip/UI/FileManager/*.ico (by Mac/scripts/make-icons.sh), and the toolbar bitmaps
CPP/7zip/UI/FileManager/*.bmp.

AI assistance
-------------
Much of the macOS port was written with AI assistance (Claude Code, by Anthropic) under the
direction of the maintainer. Commits written by an AI agent carry Co-Authored-By and
Claude-Session trailers; the working files of that process are kept in ai/.
